  "id": "formal-organizational-structure",
  "term": "formal organizational structure",
  "definition": "Formal organizational structure is the official arrangement of roles in a workplace, such as a manager-subordinate hierarchy. In the source, it is the traditional framework that separates leaders and followers by position rather than by their mutual relationship and interaction.",
